From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hayaksi1 <193020925+hayaksi1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:56:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Bring the fork's own code back under the lint rules

Everything here was invisible while the desktop type check failed first, so it
accumulated across several branches rather than being caught as it landed. The
type errors are the interesting half.

The space panel wrapped React's own setter to persist the collapsed preference,
which both narrowed it to a value-only callback the child's prop type rejects
and left a floating promise. Persisting from an effect keyed on the state
instead hands the child the real setter, so the updater form works and the
write is awaited-or-voided in one place; a first-render guard keeps it from
writing back the value it just read.

The jump-to-date control built its date-separator view model without the
roomViewStore the model now requires, so it threw on render as well as failing
the type check. It takes the store from the SDK context, like every other
caller inside the room tree, rather than the global singleton, so an embedded
room view gets its own. Its tests render the control bare and therefore now
provide that context.

The search session store moves to TypedEventEmitter, the file panel's option
role gets the aria-selected it requires, and the remaining items are unused
imports, a duplicate import, an array literal recreated on every render, and a
restricted client call in a test that already had the mock to hand.
